==English==
[[File:Hammerhead shark.jpg|thumb|''Sphyrna lewin'']]

===Etymology===
From {{compound|en|hammer|head}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|En-au-hammerhead.ogg|a=AU}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# The portion of a hammer containing the metal striking face (also including the [[claw]] or [[peen]] if so equipped).
# {{lb|en|zoology}} Any organism with head shaped like that of a hammer:
## Any [[shark]] of the family {{taxfmt|Sphyrnidae|family}}, which only includes the genera {{taxfmt|Sphyrna|genus}} and {{taxfmt|Zygaena|genus}}, with eyes set on projections from the sides of the head.
## A [[hogsucker]], a fresh-water fish of species {{taxlink|Hypentelium nigricans|species}}, in the [[sucker]] family {{taxfmt|Catostomidae|family}}.
## A {{vern|hammer-headed fruit bat}}, a fruit bat of species {{taxlink|Hypsignathus monstrosus|species}}, with a large blunt [[nozzle]].
## A [[hammerkop]], a bird of species {{taxfmt|Scopus umbretta|species}}.
# {{lb|en|slang}} A stupid person, a [[dunce]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1960|author=w:P. G. Wodehouse|title=w:Jeeves in the Offing|chapter=V
|passage=[The butler] joined us with a telegram for Bobbie on a salver. From her mother, I presumed, calling me some name which she had forgotten to insert in previous communications. Or, of course, possibly expressing once more her conviction that I was a guffin, which, I thought, having had time to ponder over it, would be something in the nature of a bohunkus or a '''hammerhead'''.}}
# A turn-around; a parking area constructed in a subdivision for initial access and construction.
# {{lb|en|biology}} A kind of [[ribozyme]]; [[hammerhead ribozyme]].
[[File:Acid_base_hammerhead_ribozyme.png|thumb|Acid-base hammerhead ribozyme]]

